{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And on the Sabbath day two lambs, etc.</b> The reason that the Sabbath additional offering is less than all the additional offerings of the new moon, the festivals, and the appointed times, is the mystical secret of the double bread (lechem mishneh), and therefore its additional offerings are two lambs corresponding to the two daily lambs, and the mystical secret of the seventhnesses is alluded to in the day itself, for it is the seventh — something in which the seventhness is not established either on the new moon or on the rest of the festivals. And although there is a seventh day of Passover, the seventhness is not fixed in it as it is on the day of the Sabbath. Understand this."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:15:43.218531417Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}